## Elves and gnomes: the three legends, the Dragonguard arsenal, surveys and the Precursor Assays (19 November 2026, implemented)

`72 - Elves and gnomes - legends, arsenal, surveys and Precursor Assays (implemented).md`: what doc 69 left waiting.
- The three legends of the ruins as Legendary Encounters: the Warden of Soara (parley with the Fleet's command-tongue),
  the Challúmaton Dragon (warded with Abjuration), the Mother of Seeds (held in Stasis); their state on the Marvels page.
- Wyrmbane: +15% in the encounters with the dragon legends.
- Unit Design: the Primary Technology Dragonguard Spellforms, eight elven blueprints and six sigils.
- Surveys abroad from the Archive's Ruin Expeditions plate (rings I-II) and the Workshop (gnomes, rings I-III).
- Hire a Precursor Archaeologist: free for the elves and the Ruinborn, open to anyone who owns a ruin.
- The gnomes' Precursor Assays: four tiles, relic samples, Assay a Relic, three Precursor patents, the Precursor view.
- Fixed on the way: the legends were tied to every ruin (now to their province); the expedition events had no
  picture (doc 69's too).
- Prompts for the three legends' pictures (section 13).
- Every check of `tools/` passes after the install (section 10).

Files:

- `tools/build_elven_arsenal.py` - the arsenal (new).
- `tools/elves2_2026-11-19/apply_elves2_2026-11-19.py` - the install, from `tools/elves2_2026-11-19/`.
- `backup_before_2026-11-19_elves2/` - the files as they were.
- `reports/apply_elves2_2026-11-19.log` - both runs, in parts; the second changed nothing.
- `previews/remnant_archive_marvels.png`, `gommo_workshop_precursor.png`, `ruin_excavation.png` - drawn from the
  generated files.
